    "result_text": "All tests pass (the suite consists of the single `AcceptanceTest`, plus its helper base classes), and `BUILD SUCCESS` confirms the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` recompiled cleanly with the new `GOLD` enum value.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier, following the existing \"capture a snapshot at creation\" pattern used by `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`, etc.\n\n**The rule:** `membershipTier` is `GOLD` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\n**Changes, each kept in its natural place:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persistent `householdSize` column (a snapshot of the household member count captured at creation, mirroring `namesakeCount`), with getter/setter. Updated `getMembershipTier()` to return `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3` (threshold as a named constant), then fall through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 captures `householdSize` at creation via a small single-responsibility helper `countHouseholdMembers(owner)`: existing owners sharing the owner's `householdId`, plus the owner itself (a household of one when `householdId` is null). This reuses the repository the same way the other counting helpers (`countNamesakes`, `countOwnersInCity`) do. Because `joinHousehold` runs before `saveOwner` in the controller, the shared `householdId` is already assigned and the sibling members are already persisted, so the count is correct.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the nullable `household_size` column. The test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the hsqldb schema change is what makes the column exist for tests; the others keep all DB variants in sync. Nullable, so the explicit-column `data.sql` seed inserts are unaffected.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (and updated its description). This is required because `OwnerDto` is generated from the spec into a typed Java enum, and MapStruct maps the entity's `String` tier into it by name \u2014 an unlisted `GOLD` would have failed.",
